  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nFor tonight, temperatures are expected to dive into the 20s to \n30s under clearing skies and calm to light flow. Therefore, a \nFreeze Warning is effect for the entire forecast area late \ntonight through early Sunday morning. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nWhile a low pressure system meanders up along the East Coast next \nweek, the Middle Ohio Valley is expected to remain dry with high \npressure in control through the end of the work week. Although \ndaytime temperatures should be right around normal for this time of \nyear, the early mornings remain chilly through mid week. If the \ngrowing season is not ended by tonight's freeze, then additional \nfrost/freeze products may be warranted late Sunday night into early \nMonday morning.",
